---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../utils/site';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Disclaimer"
  description="Disclaimer for Cozy Tiny Space — general information, approximate measurements and product limits, and rental rules."
  canonicalPath="/disclaimer/"
  breadcrumbs={[
    { name: 'Home', url: '/' },
    { name: 'Disclaimer', url: '/disclaimer/' },
  ]}
>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 pb-4 pt-10">
    <h1 class="font-display text-[clamp(2rem,5vw,3rem)] font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink">Disclaimer</h1>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[0.9rem] text-muted">Last updated: November 19, 2026</p>
    <div class="article-body mt-6">
      <h2>General information</h2>
      <p>
        The content on Cozy Tiny Space is provided for general information
        only. It is based on research, product documentation and general
        knowledge of rental living. It is not professional advice — legal,
        financial, or otherwise.
      </p>
      <h2>Measurements and product information</h2>
      <p>
        Dimensions, weight limits, prices and product availability are
        approximate and change over time. Always measure your own space and
        check the manufacturer's current specifications before buying or
        installing anything. A product that fits one rental may not fit yours.
      </p>
      <h2>Rental rules and your lease</h2>
      <p>
        Every lease is different. "Renter-friendly" and "damage-free" in our
        guides mean the method is designed to avoid permanent changes — not
        that your lease allows it. Always check your lease and, when in doubt,
        ask your landlord or property manager before installing anything,
        including adhesive products. We are not responsible for lost deposits,
        wall damage or lease disputes.
      </p>
      <h2>Weight limits and safety</h2>
      <p>
        Adhesive hooks, tension rods and removable shelves have real weight
        limits that depend on the surface, humidity, temperature and how the
        product was installed. Never hang heavy, valuable or breakable items
        above beds, seating or walkways, and never exceed the manufacturer's
        stated limit. Test every installation with a light load first.
      </p>
      <h2>Affiliate and advertising</h2>
      <p>
        This site currently contains no affiliate links. Product names appear
        as suggestions, not endorsements. See the
        <a href="/affiliate-disclosure/"> Affiliate Disclosure</a> for the
        current position.
      </p>
      <h2>External links</h2>
      <p>
        We link to third-party websites for reference. We do not control their
        content and are not responsible for it.
      </p>
      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions: <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
